On the veto: if a brief restores a column labelled 'Risk case' (a slip leg), I run the binding buffer test there as the baseline.

On the investment-grade year (2053 conservative, 2047 upside), I restate it once, to the Finance Committee, before any commitment, on any of these:
- fps deliveries below the brief's 860-940 path;
- operating profit below 15.7-16.9;
- a live quality, FAA or supply-chain problem on the ramp;
- a second development.

On the penalty: if the GM's allocation differs from my rebuild (about 0.50 PV for B's penalty), the grid governs. Nothing is netted twice.

