frame.asks_ops:
Shane, you propose the engine orders. Please bring the following.

(1) Your proposal for gtf2_solo and jv_with_rr. I expect hold/hold, the brief's only values.

(2) The Joint Venture close-out the Board asked for in round 2, as a private note to the Board. Confirm or correct each point:
(a) the gear and core remain one P&W module, with P&W design authority;
(b) there is no technology licence;
(c) GTF2's certification baseline was left untouched by the fold;
(d) the engine was ready in 2036. The bulletin confirms 2036, carried over from the folded GTF2.
Then tell me how Rolls-Royce's technology ('we are actually bringing a technology') reaches the engine. It should come only as a derivative, fully tested before its own entry into service, never touching the gear and core and never through a licence. Tell me whether the integrated-team rule [P-1240] still holds with two partners' content.

(3) A fleet report, not a readiness report.
- Cover the Joint Venture engine on NGSA since 2037 and the GTF fleet: time on wing, LLP life, shop visits and AOG, from measured data.
- If the brief holds none, say so plainly and give no figure. My dated recoveries have slipped before [PX-0098][PX-0104], and so have yours.
- If any durability or safety-critical-part finding exists, it goes to Governance and Public Policy and the full Board before the 2050 orders.

(4) Pacing parts and capacity. Give me the order of call between:
- GTF fleet MRO;
- support for the new engine fleet on NGSA;
- A320neo engine deliveries;
- new-engine production.
Cover powder metal (records discipline [P-1040]), castings and MRO slots. Engines on the board fall from 990 (2039) to 863 (2049 on). Tell me whether that frees capacity for the fleet, and say so without inventing a count.

(5) Engineering load. With no programme spend left, what remains:
- the Hot Section kit at shop visits;
- Joint Venture derivative work;
- fleet support.
Is any of it pulling engineers off the fleet?

(6) Your two veto checks on hold/hold and on the other moves:
- ground 1, durability before entry into service;
- ground 2, parts and capacity for the fleet.

(7) Check my draft statement against your rules:
- no durability claim beyond the fleet record;
- no dated AOG recovery;
- no airframer dates, rates or shares;
- no programme cost figures.

